---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const lastUpdated = 'October 9, 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Service"
  description="Terms of Service for using CodesCompiler educational content, tutorials, examples, and tools."
>
  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto py-12 px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 bg-white shadow-sm my-8 rounded-lg">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-extrabold text-gray-900 mb-4">Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-8"><strong>Last Updated:</strong> {lastUpdated}</p>

    <div class="prose prose-brand prose-lg max-w-none">
      <h2>1. Acceptance of These Terms</h2>
      <p>
        By accessing or using CodesCompiler, you agree to these Terms of Service and our
        <a href="/privacy-policy/">Privacy Policy</a>. If you do not agree with these terms,
        please do not use the website.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Educational Content</h2>
      <p>
        CodesCompiler provides tutorials, programming examples, definitions, articles,
        references, and interactive tools for educational and informational purposes.
        Content may be updated, changed, or removed as technologies and best practices evolve.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Use of Code Examples</h2>
      <p>
        Code examples are intended for learning and experimentation. You are responsible for
        reviewing, testing, securing, and adapting any code before using it in a production
        environment.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Intellectual Property</h2>
      <p>
        Unless otherwise stated, the original text, graphics, branding, and website design
        published by CodesCompiler are protected by applicable intellectual-property laws.
        Individual code examples may be used for learning and incorporated into your own
        projects, subject to any license or attribution stated on the relevant page.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Prohibited Use</h2>
      <p>
        You must not use the website to distribute malware, attack or disrupt services,
        attempt unauthorized access, abuse interactive tools, scrape the service in a way
        that causes harm, or violate applicable laws.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Third-Party Services and Links</h2>
      <p>
        The website may include third-party advertisements, links, tools, or services.
        Third-party services are governed by their own terms and policies. CodesCompiler
        does not control and is not responsible for third-party services.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Disclaimer and Limitation</h2>
      <p>
        CodesCompiler is provided on an "as is" and "as available" basis. We do not guarantee
        that the website or its content will always be accurate, complete, uninterrupted,
        secure, or free of errors.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Changes to These Terms</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these Terms of Service from time to time. The updated version will be
        posted on this page and will include a revised "Last Updated" date.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Contact Us</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about these Terms can be sent to
        <a href="mailto:contact@codescompiler.com">contact@codescompiler.com</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
